title: barbarian_encounter
---
Narrator:
The system reads as contested before your ships are in range.

---

Narrator:
Not by any faction on your charts.

The transponder signatures are wrong — pre-standard, almost organic in their irregularity. Someone is broadcasting on frequencies that haven't been in use since before the Compact.

---

Narrator:
Your lead vessel crosses the threshold and the chatter stops.

Then, without warning, a single vessel detaches from the debris field and holds position directly across your approach vector. It makes no aggressive move. It simply waits.

---

Narrator:
Your signals officer translates the broadcast as best she can. It is not a language. It is closer to a liturgy.

Something is being worshipped here.

Something old.

---

-> [Open a channel — offer tribute]
    <<apply_effect "horde_tribute">>
    <<chain_event "barbarian_ritual">>
    Narrator:
    You broadcast on their frequency. Food stores. Fuel cells. Whatever they want.

    Narrator:
    The vessel holds for a long moment. Then it withdraws.

    Narrator:
    Your signals officer marks the system. She doesn't say what she's thinking.

    Narrator:
    You paid. They accepted. The hordes pull back — for now.

-> [Refuse to yield — push through]
    <<apply_effect "horde_aggression">>
    <<chain_event "barbarian_ritual">>
    Narrator:
    You give the order. Your ships accelerate.

    Narrator:
    The lone vessel doesn't move until you're almost on top of it.

    Narrator:
    Then it screams — not a signal, not a weapon — a sound, somehow, broadcast on every frequency at once.

    Narrator:
    The horde answers.

    Narrator:
    You'll be fighting your way through every system they claim from here on.

===
